From 4d8472ce41df4ed156066d5c0b98be4f9c3dc0cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Gonzalez <dev@gonzalezerik.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:23:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] bsps/powerpc/ibookg3: Prepare for the real iBook

Add a text console on the frame buffer Open Firmware set up, since the
iBook has no external serial port.  On 8-bit displays it sets two
palette entries through Open Firmware before leaving it.

Program the trigger of each OpenPIC source from the device tree: Apple
interrupt specifiers mark sources as level (active low) or edge.  QEMU
does not care, the hardware does.

Read device tree properties correctly: getprop returns the full length
of a property, which the checks for the PCI bridge and ATA registers
did not allow for.  Find the ATA controllers by their compatible
property, as they are ata-3 or ata-4 depending on the machine.

Let applications set the load address with IBOOKG3_LOAD_BASE, so that
an image for Open Firmware loads where it runs.
---
